proofs.proof_tex:
The upper and lower bounds concern the same law class \(\mathcal M_n\) and the same public-information decision class \(\mathcal T_n\).  By thm:clipped-absolute-upper and def:absolute-risk,
\[
\mathfrak R_n^{(1)}
\le\sup_{\mathcal M_n}E_P|\widehat\tau_{\lambda_n^\star}-\tau(P)|
\le C\rho_n.                                                  \tag{49}
\]
For \(n\ge5\), every block size \(m_j\) in def:median-estimator satisfies \(n/9\le m_j\le n\).  Applying the equation-by-equation bound proved in thm:clipped-absolute-upper to a block, while retaining the full-sample threshold specified in def:median-estimator, changes each sampling scale by at most a class constant:
\[
m_j^{-1/2}\le3n^{-1/2},
m_j^{-1/(\kappa+1)}\asymp n^{-1/(\kappa+1)},
(m_jr_{1n}^2)^{-1}\asymp(nr_{1n}^2)^{-1},                   \tag{50}
\]
and the propensity-error scale is unchanged.  Hence every independent block copy has mean absolute error at most \(K\rho_n\), uniformly over \(\mathcal M_n\).  Lem:median-risk-upgrade gives
\[
\sup_{\mathcal M_n}
\{E_P(\widehat\tau_{\mathrm{med}}-\tau(P))^2\}^{1/2}
\le\sqrt{21}\,K\rho_n.                                    \tag{51}
\]
For \(1\le n<5\), def:oracle-threshold gives \(\lambda_n^\star\ge\min\{\lambda_0,1/4\}\), and ass:right-overlap bounds the control denominator away from zero.  Ass:outcome-second-moment and conditional Jensen imply \(E_P[g_0(X)^2]\le M_Y/\eta_+\).  Ass:bounded-treatment-effect-signal then gives \(E_P[g_1(X)^2]\le2M+2M_Y/\eta_+\).  The three radius certificates and \(r_{an}\le\bar r\) therefore bound the second moment of the full-sample clipped score uniformly.  Since \(\rho_n\ge n^{-1/2}\ge1/2\) for these four sample sizes, (51) remains valid after increasing \(K\).  Def:root-mse-risk now yields \(\mathfrak R_n^{(2)}\le C\rho_n\).

For fixed \(\delta\in(0,1/4)\), the probability assertion of thm:clipped-absolute-upper and def:probability-risk give
\[
\mathfrak R_{n,\delta}^{(\mathrm{prob})}\le C_\delta\rho_n. \tag{52}
\]
Conversely, thm:four-channel-converse gives the absolute-risk and root-mean-squared-risk lower bounds and, for every \(T\in\mathcal T_n\),
\[
\sup_{\mathcal M_n}P\{|T-\tau(P)|\ge c\rho_n\}\ge\delta_0. \tag{53}
\]
If \(0<\delta\le\delta_0\) and \(u<c\rho_n\), then
\[
\sup_{\mathcal M_n}P\{|T-\tau(P)|>u\}
\ge\sup_{\mathcal M_n}P\{|T-\tau(P)|\ge c\rho_n\}
\ge\delta_0\ge\delta.                                      \tag{54}
\]
Taking the two infima in def:probability-risk gives \(\mathfrak R_{n,\delta}^{(\mathrm{prob})}\ge c\rho_n\).  Combining (49)--(54) with the two loss lower bounds proves all three uniform equivalences.
